# Git Flow + Commitizen

Always follow **Git Flow** for branches and **Commitizen / Conventional Commits** for messages.

**Never commit directly to `master`/`main` or `develop`.** All changes reach these branches **only via PR** (Github PR for the fork `vs-76/quickfast`). Never push the feature/fix branch directly into `develop`/`master`; open a PR and let it be merged.

- All work happens on side branches (`feature/`, `bugfix/`, `hotfix/`, `release/`); commits go on those branches and nowhere else.
- No `git checkout develop && git commit` / `git commit` while on `develop`/`master`/`main`. If asked to commit on a protected branch, stop, warn, and switch to a feature branch.
- "Merge into" targets below describe the PR that merges that branch, not direct commits.

## Branching (Git Flow)

| Purpose | Branch from | Branch name | Merge into |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| New feature | `develop` | `feature/<short-name>` | `develop` |
| Non-urgent bugfix | `develop` | `bugfix/<short-name>` | `develop` |
| Production hotfix | `master` | `hotfix/<short-name>` | `master` **and** `develop` |
| Release prep | `develop` | `release/<x.y.z>` | `master` **and** `develop` |

- Default working base is `develop`.
- Tag releases on `master` after a release/hotfix merge (`vX.Y.Z`).
- Do not invent ad-hoc branch names (`fix`, `wip`, bare ticket IDs alone).

```bash
# ✅ feature work
git checkout develop && git pull
git checkout -b feature/decoder-timeout
# ... commit on feature/decoder-timeout ...
git push -u origin feature/decoder-timeout   # then open PR to develop (or master for hotfix)

# ❌ wrong
git checkout -b my-fix
git commit            # on develop/master directly
git push origin develop
```

## Commits (Commitizen)

Use Conventional Commits. Prefer `git cz` / `cz commit` when available; otherwise write the same format by hand.

```
<type>(<optional-scope>): <imperative summary>

[optional body]

[optional footer]
```

**Types:** `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`

**Rules:**
- Summary ≤ ~72 chars, imperative (“add”, not “added”), no trailing period
- Scope optional but preferred when clear (`codec`, `decoder`, `docs`)
- Breaking change: `!` after type/scope **or** `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer
- One logical change per commit; do not mix unrelated edits

```
# ✅
feat(decoder): add template version guard
fix(codec): handle empty presence map
docs: clarify Git Flow merge targets

# ❌
Updated stuff
WIP
fixed bug
```

When the user asks to commit, draft a Commitizen-style message and follow the repo’s existing commit-message user rules (HEREDOC, no amend unless allowed, etc.).
